{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2596 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "971dec2b4446cfeb54f1790d15755261e6c99efa361a0da6824ed499345eb10b" :edb/db-before-t 2595 :edb/db-after-t 2596 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535908 50 #inst "2026-10-15T06:23:11.824Z" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186179646 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540271 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186179646 1040 #edb/ref 17592186540276 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540269 1080 "10" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540269 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540269 1083 #uuid "0d90ae4b-bf36-5b82-b2be-e660abeed08c" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540270 1080 "0" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540270 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540270 1083 #uuid "30be5477-8759-5e18-b8b5-083d35cf6932" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540271 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540272 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540271 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540271 1071 "![](images/e4/e46488d991bf461eacc51ecfcd490497bf13fcdf2b7ff998b54fdc501caf40ab.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=3\\,i$ and a square $C$ with side length $10$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540271 1072 #uuid "35cb0fe5-8d22-5821-8dbb-8da5656983ba" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540271 1074 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere the sides ${C}_{i}$ and unit vectors ${n}_{i}$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/a2/a2964076c4126d6277625260c45479d1a4fb2028f7e75223a0f5942b15f5a2d2.png)\n\nNow, since the vector field $F=3\\,i$ is parallel to ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{4},$ there is zero net flow through these two sides. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nSo, our expression for the flux reduces to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, since the vector field is uniform, the net outflow through ${C}_{1}$ will cancel with the net inflow through ${C}_{3}.$ That is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s=-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s\\,⟹\\,{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540269 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540270 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540273 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540274 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540275 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1077 "selection" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540270 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540272 1079 #uuid "807c5f44-a0c5-5774-a41c-61960d9dc9e4" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540273 1080 "30" 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540273 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535908 17592186045443 true] [17592186540273 1083 #uuid "a2569f81-23d6-57a6-8c40-9db98a155401" 13194139